s": 2, "created_at": "2017-12-06T08:45:23Z", "updated_at": "2018-07-09T09:04:06Z", "closed_at": "2017-12-07T07:34:07Z", "assignee": null, "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "I did\r\n```\r\n$ make clean\r\n$ sudo make default install\r\n$ cd example/takeoff_land\r\n$ mkdir build\r\n$ cd build\r\n$ cmake ..\r\n$ make\r\n$ ./takeoff_land => leads to runtime error\r\n./takeoff_and_land: error while loading shared libraries: libdronecore.so: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nHowever, after I export `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`, it works well.\r\n```\r\n$ export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib/\r\n$ ./takeoff_and_land \r\nWaiting to discover device...\r\n[01:55:17|Info ] New device on: 127.0.0.1:14557 (udp_connection.cpp:211)\r\n[01:55:17|Info ] Applying default FollowMe configuration FollowMe to the device... (follow_me_impl.cpp:182)\r\n[01:55:17|Debug] MAVLink: info: data link #0 lost (device_impl.cpp:229)\r\n[01:55:17|Debug] MAVLink: info: data link #0 regained (device_impl.cpp:229)\r\n[01:55:18|Debug] Discovered 4294967298 (dronecore_impl.cpp:234)\r\nDiscovered device with UUID: 4294967298\r\n...\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think we need to change `CMakeLists.txt` during installing dronecore library.\r\nIt seems [this](https://github.com/dronecore/DroneCore/blob/develop/CMakeLists.txt#L192) line in CMakeLists.txt doesn't have effect of exporting dronecore library path.\r\n\r\nShouldn't we instruct user to export this if not done already ?\r\n", "closed_by": {"login": "shakthi-prashanth-m", "id": 26615772, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2NjE1Nzcy", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26615772?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/shakthi-prashanth-m", "html_u